---
import { Font } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { AiHubPage } from "@/page-bodies/ai-hub-index";

/* THE SHELL IS BACK ON, as of 2026-09-09. This page was built with
   `chrome={false}` so the story could decide its own top and bottom before the
   navigation did, which was right while it was being composed and is no longer:
   it is a page of the site and the reader needs the site's own way in and out
   of it. The navbar is fixed at z-[70], above the opening line's overlay at
   z-30 and the foreground copy at z-40, so it sits over the story rather than
   inside it and nothing on the page had to move.

   PLACEHOLDER META. The title and description below are holding the shape of
   the tags, not stating the page's copy. Neither is written yet and neither is
   invented here. */

const HREF = "/ai-hub";
---

<Base
  title="AI Hub | ENH Marketing"
  description="ENH Marketing's AI Hub."
  canonical={HREF}
>
  {/* Space Grotesk is this page's typeface and no other page's. Declaring it
      here rather than in Base.astro is what keeps the preload off the other
      141 pages. */}
  <Font slot="head" cssVariable="--font-grotesk" preload />

  {/* THIS PAGE IS DARK WHATEVER THE READER'S THEME. It is a photograph of a
      night mountain that becomes deep space: every surface on it is painted
      black or near-black in the markup rather than through a theme token,
      because those tokens are near-black in dark and near-white in light and
      the story cannot follow them. The shell can, though, and until now did:
      with the site in light mode the navbar and footer came up pale at the top
      and bottom of a black page.

      So the class is set here, in the head, after the layout's own theme script
      and before first paint, which is why there is no flash. localStorage is
      deliberately not written: this is what one page looks like, not a change
      to what the reader chose for the site. */}
  <script slot="head" is:inline>
    document.documentElement.classList.add("dark");
  </script>
  <AiHubPage client:load />
</Base>
